From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zaid <nottzaid@tutamail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:57:35 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 06/12] miles-bench S16: render-thread CPU cuts

- Frame trace: count draws per command list and add them to the frame
  in ExecuteCommandLists, not one global atomic per draw.
- Index cache: bind the cache buffer once per command buffer and select
  each cached draw's indices with firstIndex; the shadow of that binding
  is cleared wherever the index binding or command buffer can change.
- Clear keep: a use repeating the list's last use of a heap returns
  before taking the clear-keep lock.
- Fences: GetCompletedValue reads the value with an acquire load and no
  mutex; the runtime stores are release stores under the mutex.
- Index cache: reader/writer lock; hits on fresh runs are served under
  the shared lock, run_last raised with a CAS max (review fix).

All lossless: identical GPU work and D3D12-visible behaviour.
